IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc2-nuclear-prize-fights.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), PART II, ss 82.2 to 83: nuclear material, radioactive material and devices (ss 82.2 to 82.7) and prize fights (s 83).
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30);
-- it is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words) / NOTHING (not covered): see the header of ccc2-treason.l4 and NOTES.md.
-- "nuclear material", "radioactive material" and "nuclear facility" are s 2's terms: their answers are seam inputs (MAYBE BOOLEAN). "device" is section 82.2's own.

§ `Section 82.2 -- Definition of device`

-- "For the purposes of sections 82.3 to 82.5, device means any of the following: (a) a nuclear explosive device; (b) a device that disperses radioactive material; (c) a device that emits ionizing radiation
-- and that is capable of causing death, serious bodily harm or substantial damage to property or the environment." A closed "means any of the following" definition (JUST FALSE outside it).
-- src:1219 | Definition of device
-- src:1220 | 82.2 For the purposes of sections 82.3 to 82.5, device means any of the following:
-- src:1221 | (a) a nuclear explosive device;
-- src:1222 | (b) a device that disperses radioactive material;
-- src:1223 | (c) a device that emits ionizing radiation and that is capable of causing death, serious bodily harm or substantial damage to property or the environment.
@ref Criminal Code s 82.2 (definition of device) (src:1219-1223)
DECLARE `s 82.2 kind of device` IS ONE OF
    `s 82.2(a) a nuclear explosive device`
    `s 82.2(b) a device that disperses radioactive material`
    `s 82.2(c) a device that emits ionizing radiation`
    `s 82.2 a device of none of those kinds`

@ref Criminal Code s 82.2 (definition of device) (src:1219-1223)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 82.2 kind of device`
      `s 2 radioactive material: the material the device disperses is radioactive material` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the device that emits ionizing radiation is capable of causing death, serious bodily harm or substantial damage to property or the environment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 82.2 the thing is a device for the purposes of sections 82.3 to 82.5` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 82.2(a) a nuclear explosive device` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 82.2(b) a device that disperses radioactive material` THEN `s 2 radioactive material: the material the device disperses is radioactive material`   -- JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE ("device means any of the following"); NOTHING as s 2 answers
    WHEN `s 82.2(c) a device that emits ionizing radiation` THEN
        IF `the device that emits ionizing radiation is capable of causing death, serious bodily harm or substantial damage to property or the environment`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "device means any of the following: ... (c) a device that emits ionizing radiation and that is capable of causing death, serious bodily harm or substantial damage to property or the environment"
    WHEN `s 82.2 a device of none of those kinds` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "device means any of the following"

§ `Sections 82.3 to 82.7 -- Nuclear material, radioactive material and devices`

-- Section 82.3: "Everyone who, with intent to cause death, serious bodily harm or substantial damage to property or the environment, makes a device or possesses, uses, transfers, exports, imports, alters or
-- disposes of nuclear material, radioactive material or a device or commits an act against a nuclear facility or an act that causes serious interference with or serious disruption of its operations, is guilty
-- of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for life."
-- src:1224 | Possession, etc., of nuclear material, radioactive material or device
-- src:1225 | 82.3 Everyone who, with intent to cause death, serious bodily harm or substantial damage to property or the environment, makes a device or possesses, uses, transfers, exports, imports, alters or disposes of nuclear material, radioactive material or a device or commits an act against a nuclear facility or an act that causes serious interference with or serious disruption of its operations, is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for life.
@ref Criminal Code s 82.3 (possession, etc., of nuclear material, radioactive material or device) (src:1224-1225)
DECLARE `s 82.3 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 82.3 makes a device`
    `s 82.3 possesses, uses, transfers, exports, imports, alters or disposes of nuclear material`
    `s 82.3 possesses, uses, transfers, exports, imports, alters or disposes of radioactive material`
    `s 82.3 possesses, uses, transfers, exports, imports, alters or disposes of a device`
    `s 82.3 commits an act against a nuclear facility`
    `s 82.3 commits an act that causes serious interference with or serious disruption of the operations of a nuclear facility`
    `s 82.3 another act`

@ref Criminal Code s 82.3 (possession, etc., of nuclear material, radioactive material or device) (src:1224-1225)
GIVEN act IS A `s 82.3 act`
      `the person acts with intent to cause death, serious bodily harm or substantial damage to property or the environment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 nuclear material: the thing is nuclear material` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2 radioactive material: the thing is radioactive material` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 82.2 the thing is a device: the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2 nuclear facility: the thing is a nuclear facility` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 82.3 the person commits the offence of possessing or using nuclear material, radioactive material or a device with intent to harm` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF act EQUALS `s 82.3 another act` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "makes a device or possesses, uses, transfers, exports, imports, alters or disposes of nuclear material, radioactive material or a device or commits an act against a nuclear facility"
        IF `the object answer` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the s 2 and s 82.2 definitions ("nuclear material means", "radioactive material means", "nuclear facility means", "device means any of the following") say the thing is not within the section
        IF `the person acts with intent to cause death, serious bodily harm or substantial damage to property or the environment` AND `the object answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with intent to cause death, serious bodily harm or substantial damage to property or the environment"
    WHERE
        `the object answer` MEANS
            CONSIDER act
            WHEN `s 82.3 makes a device` THEN `s 82.2 the thing is a device: the answer`
            WHEN `s 82.3 possesses, uses, transfers, exports, imports, alters or disposes of nuclear material` THEN `s 2 nuclear material: the thing is nuclear material`
            WHEN `s 82.3 possesses, uses, transfers, exports, imports, alters or disposes of radioactive material` THEN `s 2 radioactive material: the thing is radioactive material`
            WHEN `s 82.3 possesses, uses, transfers, exports, imports, alters or disposes of a device` THEN `s 82.2 the thing is a device: the answer`
            WHEN `s 82.3 commits an act against a nuclear facility` THEN `s 2 nuclear facility: the thing is a nuclear facility`
            WHEN `s 82.3 commits an act that causes serious interference with or serious disruption of the operations of a nuclear facility` THEN `s 2 nuclear facility: the thing is a nuclear facility`
            WHEN `s 82.3 another act` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the section names the acts it covers and does not say no to any other act

@ref Criminal Code s 82.3 (punishment) (src:1224-1225)
`s 82.3 the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref Criminal Code s 82.3 (punishment) (src:1224-1225)
`s 82.3 the punishment` MEANS
    LIST Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for life`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- Section 82.4: "Everyone who, with intent to compel a person, government or international organization to do or refrain from doing any act, uses or alters nuclear material, radioactive material or a device or
-- commits an act against a nuclear facility or an act that causes serious interference with or serious disruption of its operations, is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for life."
-- src:1226 | Use or alteration of nuclear material, radioactive material or device
-- src:1227 | 82.4 Everyone who, with intent to compel a person, government or international organization to do or refrain from doing any act, uses or alters nuclear material, radioactive material or a device or commits an act against a nuclear facility or an act that causes serious interference with or serious disruption of its operations, is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for life.
@ref Criminal Code s 82.4 (use or alteration of nuclear material, radioactive material or device) (src:1226-1227)
DECLARE `s 82.4 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 82.4 uses or alters nuclear material`
    `s 82.4 uses or alters radioactive material`
    `s 82.4 uses or alters a device`
    `s 82.4 commits an act against a nuclear facility`
    `s 82.4 commits an act that causes serious interference with or serious disruption of the operations of a nuclear facility`
    `s 82.4 another act`

@ref Criminal Code s 82.4 (use or alteration of nuclear material, radioactive material or device) (src:1226-1227)
GIVEN act IS A `s 82.4 act`
      `the person acts with intent to compel a person, government or international organization to do or refrain from doing any act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 nuclear material: the thing is nuclear material` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2 radioactive material: the thing is radioactive material` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 82.2 the thing is a device: the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2 nuclear facility: the thing is a nuclear facility` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 82.4 the person commits the offence of using or altering nuclear material, radioactive material or a device to compel` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF act EQUALS `s 82.4 another act` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "uses or alters nuclear material, radioactive material or a device or commits an act against a nuclear facility"
        IF `the object answer` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the s 2 and s 82.2 definitions ("nuclear material means", "radioactive material means", "nuclear facility means", "device means any of the following") say the thing is not within the section
        IF `the person acts with intent to compel a person, government or international organization to do or refrain from doing any act` AND `the object answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with intent to compel a person, government or international organization to do or refrain from doing any act"
    WHERE
        `the object answer` MEANS
            CONSIDER act
            WHEN `s 82.4 uses or alters nuclear material` THEN `s 2 nuclear material: the thing is nuclear material`
            WHEN `s 82.4 uses or alters radioactive material` THEN `s 2 radioactive material: the thing is radioactive material`
            WHEN `s 82.4 uses or alters a device` THEN `s 82.2 the thing is a device: the answer`
            WHEN `s 82.4 commits an act against a nuclear facility` THEN `s 2 nuclear facility: the thing is a nuclear facility`
            WHEN `s 82.4 commits an act that causes serious interference with or serious disruption of the operations of a nuclear facility` THEN `s 2 nuclear facility: the thing is a nuclear facility`
            WHEN `s 82.4 another act` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the section names the acts it covers and does not say no to any other act

@ref Criminal Code s 82.4 (punishment) (src:1226-1227)
`s 82.4 the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref Criminal Code s 82.4 (punishment) (src:1226-1227)
`s 82.4 the punishment` MEANS
    LIST Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for life`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- Section 82.5: "Everyone who commits an indictable offence under this or any other Act of Parliament, with intent to obtain nuclear material, radioactive material or a device or to obtain access to a nuclear
-- facility, is guilty of an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for life." The class of the offence committed is taken as the answer of the part that owns it (a `Class of offence`): an indictable
-- offence qualifies; a dual-procedure offence is not named by the text and is NOTHING (fork F14).
-- src:1228 | Commission of indictable offence to obtain nuclear material, etc.
-- src:1229 | 82.5 Everyone who commits an indictable offence under this or any other Act of Parliament, with intent to obtain nuclear material, radioactive material or a device or to obtain access to a nuclear facility, is guilty of an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for life.
@ref Criminal Code s 82.5 (commission of indictable offence to obtain nuclear material, etc.) (src:1228-1229)
DECLARE `s 82.5 object of the intent` IS ONE OF
    `s 82.5 to obtain nuclear material`
    `s 82.5 to obtain radioactive material`
    `s 82.5 to obtain a device`
    `s 82.5 to obtain access to a nuclear facility`
    `s 82.5 another object`

@ref Criminal Code s 82.5 (commission of indictable offence to obtain nuclear material, etc.) (src:1228-1229)
GIVEN `the class of the offence the person commits under this or any other Act of Parliament` IS A `Class of offence`
      object IS A `s 82.5 object of the intent`
      `s 2 nuclear material: the thing is nuclear material` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2 radioactive material: the thing is radioactive material` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 82.2 the thing is a device: the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2 nuclear facility: the thing is a nuclear facility` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 82.5 the person commits an indictable offence with intent to obtain nuclear material, radioactive material or a device, or access to a nuclear facility` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF object EQUALS `s 82.5 another object` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with intent to obtain nuclear material, radioactive material or a device or to obtain access to a nuclear facility"
        IF `the object answer` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the s 2 and s 82.2 definitions say the thing is not within the section
        IF `the class of the offence the person commits under this or any other Act of Parliament` EQUALS `an indictable offence` AND `the object answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Everyone who commits an indictable offence under this or any other Act of Parliament"
    WHERE
        `the object answer` MEANS
            CONSIDER object
            WHEN `s 82.5 to obtain nuclear material` THEN `s 2 nuclear material: the thing is nuclear material`
            WHEN `s 82.5 to obtain radioactive material` THEN `s 2 radioactive material: the thing is radioactive material`
            WHEN `s 82.5 to obtain a device` THEN `s 82.2 the thing is a device: the answer`
            WHEN `s 82.5 to obtain access to a nuclear facility` THEN `s 2 nuclear facility: the thing is a nuclear facility`
            WHEN `s 82.5 another object` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the section names the objects it covers and does not say no to any other object

@ref Criminal Code s 82.5 (punishment) (src:1228-1229)
`s 82.5 the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref Criminal Code s 82.5 (punishment) (src:1228-1229)
`s 82.5 the punishment` MEANS
    LIST Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for life`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- Section 82.6: "Everyone who threatens to commit an offence under any of sections 82.3 to 82.5 is guilty of an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years."
-- The offence threatened is tested by its section number (PLAN.md seam rule R1): 82.3 to 82.5 in the Code's order.
-- src:1230 | Threats
-- src:1231 | 82.6 Everyone who threatens to commit an offence under any of sections 82.3 to 82.5 is guilty of an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years.
@ref Criminal Code s 82.6 (threats) (src:1230-1231)
GIVEN `the person threatens to commit the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence threatened` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 82.6 the person threatens to commit an offence under any of sections 82.3 to 82.5` MEANS
    IF `the person threatens to commit the offence` AND `the offence threatened`'s `section` AT LEAST 82.3 AND `the offence threatened`'s `section` AT MOST 82.5
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Everyone who threatens to commit an offence under any of sections 82.3 to 82.5"

@ref Criminal Code s 82.6 (punishment) (src:1230-1231)
`s 82.6 the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref Criminal Code s 82.6 (punishment) (src:1230-1231)
`s 82.6 the punishment` MEANS
    LIST Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- Section 82.7: "For greater certainty, sections 82.3 to 82.6 do not apply to an act that is committed during an armed conflict and that, at the time and in the place of its commission, is in accordance with
-- customary international law or conventional international law applicable to the conflict, or to activities undertaken by military forces of a state in the exercise of their official duties, to the extent
-- that those activities are governed by other rules of international law." A flat negative (JUST FALSE).
-- src:1232 | Armed forces
-- src:1233 | 82.7 For greater certainty, sections 82.3 to 82.6 do not apply to an act that is committed during an armed conflict and that, at the time and in the place of its commission, is in accordance with customary international law or conventional international law applicable to the conflict, or to activities undertaken by military forces of a state in the exercise of their official duties, to the extent that those activities are governed by other rules of international law.
@ref Criminal Code s 82.7 (armed forces) (src:1232-1233)
GIVEN `the act is committed during an armed conflict` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time and in the place of its commission it is in accordance with customary international law or conventional international law applicable to the conflict` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activity is undertaken by military forces of a state in the exercise of their official duties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those activities are governed by other rules of international law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 82.7 sections 82.3 to 82.6 apply to the act` MEANS
    IF (`the act is committed during an armed conflict` AND `at the time and in the place of its commission it is in accordance with customary international law or conventional international law applicable to the conflict`)
        OR (`the activity is undertaken by military forces of a state in the exercise of their official duties` AND `those activities are governed by other rules of international law`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "sections 82.3 to 82.6 do not apply to an act that is committed during an armed conflict and that, at the time and in the place of its commission, is in accordance with customary international law or conventional international law applicable to the conflict, or to activities undertaken by military forces of a state in the exercise of their official duties, to the extent that those activities are governed by other rules of international law"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 82.7 says where the sections do not apply, not where they do

§ `Section 83 -- Prize fights`

-- Subsection (2): "In this section, prize fight means an encounter or fight with fists, hands or feet between two persons who have met for that purpose by previous arrangement made by or for them, but does not
-- include (a) a contest between amateur athletes in a combative sport with fists, hands or feet held in a province if the sport is on the programme of the International Olympic Committee or the International
-- Paralympic Committee and, in the case where the province's lieutenant governor in council or any other person or body specified by him or her requires it, the contest is held with their permission; (b) ... if the
-- sport has been designated by the province's lieutenant governor in council or by any other person or body specified by him or her and, in the case where [that person or body] requires it, the contest is held with
-- their permission; (c) ... held in a province with the permission of the province's lieutenant governor in council or any other person or body specified by him or her; and (d) a boxing contest or mixed martial arts
-- contest held in a province with the permission or under the authority of an athletic board, commission or similar body established by or under the authority of the province's legislature for the control of sport
-- within the province." A closed "means" definition with four flat-negative exclusions (JUST FALSE).
-- src:1242 | Definition of prize fight
-- src:1243 | (2) In this section, prize fight means an encounter or fight with fists, hands or feet between two persons who have met for that purpose by previous arrangement made by or for them, but does not include
-- src:1244 | (a) a contest between amateur athletes in a combative sport with fists, hands or feet held in a province if the sport is on the programme of the International Olympic Committee or the International Paralympic Committee and, in the case where the province’s lieutenant governor in council or any other person or body specified by him or her requires it, the contest is held with their permission;
-- src:1245 | (b) a contest between amateur athletes in a combative sport with fists, hands or feet held in a province if the sport has been designated by the province’s lieutenant governor in council or by any other person or body specified by him or her and, in the case where the lieutenant governor in council or other specified person or body requires it, the contest is held with their permission;
-- src:1246 | (c) a contest between amateur athletes in a combative sport with fists, hands or feet held in a province with the permission of the province’s lieutenant governor in council or any other person or body specified by him or her; and
-- src:1247 | (d) a boxing contest or mixed martial arts contest held in a province with the permission or under the authority of an athletic board, commission or similar body established by or under the authority of the province’s legislature for the control of sport within the province.
@ref Criminal Code s 83(2) (definition of prize fight) (src:1242-1247)
GIVEN `it is an encounter or fight with fists, hands or feet` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is between two persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the two persons have met for that purpose by previous arrangement made by or for them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a contest between amateur athletes in a combative sport with fists, hands or feet held in a province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sport is on the programme of the International Olympic Committee or the International Paralympic Committee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sport has been designated by the province's lieutenant governor in council or by any other person or body specified by him or her` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the province's lieutenant governor in council or other person or body requires permission for the contest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contest is held with their permission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a boxing contest or mixed martial arts contest held in a province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is held with the permission or under the authority of an athletic board, commission or similar body established by or under the authority of the province's legislature for the control of sport within the province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83(2) the encounter is a prize fight` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `it is an encounter or fight with fists, hands or feet`) OR (NOT `it is between two persons`) OR (NOT `the two persons have met for that purpose by previous arrangement made by or for them`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "prize fight means an encounter or fight with fists, hands or feet between two persons who have met for that purpose by previous arrangement made by or for them"
        IF `excluded by paragraph (a)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include (a) a contest between amateur athletes in a combative sport with fists, hands or feet held in a province if the sport is on the programme of the International Olympic Committee or the International Paralympic Committee"
        IF `excluded by paragraph (b)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include ... (b) a contest between amateur athletes in a combative sport with fists, hands or feet held in a province if the sport has been designated"
        IF `excluded by paragraph (c)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include ... (c) a contest between amateur athletes in a combative sport with fists, hands or feet held in a province with the permission of the province's lieutenant governor in council"
        IF `excluded by paragraph (d)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include ... (d) a boxing contest or mixed martial arts contest held in a province with the permission or under the authority of an athletic board"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `permission is not required or is given` MEANS (NOT `the province's lieutenant governor in council or other person or body requires permission for the contest`) OR `the contest is held with their permission`
        `excluded by paragraph (a)` MEANS `it is a contest between amateur athletes in a combative sport with fists, hands or feet held in a province` AND `the sport is on the programme of the International Olympic Committee or the International Paralympic Committee` AND `permission is not required or is given`
        `excluded by paragraph (b)` MEANS `it is a contest between amateur athletes in a combative sport with fists, hands or feet held in a province` AND `the sport has been designated by the province's lieutenant governor in council or by any other person or body specified by him or her` AND `permission is not required or is given`
        `excluded by paragraph (c)` MEANS `it is a contest between amateur athletes in a combative sport with fists, hands or feet held in a province` AND `the contest is held with their permission`
        `excluded by paragraph (d)` MEANS `it is a boxing contest or mixed martial arts contest held in a province` AND `it is held with the permission or under the authority of an athletic board, commission or similar body established by or under the authority of the province's legislature for the control of sport within the province`

-- Subsection (1): "Every one who (a) engages as a principal in a prize fight, (b) advises, encourages or promotes a prize fight, or (c) is present at a prize fight as an aid, second, surgeon, umpire, backer or
-- reporter, is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction."
-- src:1236 | Engaging in prize fight
-- src:1237 | 83 (1) Every one who
-- src:1238 | (a) engages as a principal in a prize fight,
-- src:1239 | (b) advises, encourages or promotes a prize fight, or
-- src:1240 | (c) is present at a prize fight as an aid, second, surgeon, umpire, backer or reporter,
-- src:1241 | is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 83(1) (engaging in prize fight) (src:1236-1241)
DECLARE `s 83(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 83(1)(a) engages as a principal in a prize fight`
    `s 83(1)(b) advises, encourages or promotes a prize fight`
    `s 83(1)(c) is present at a prize fight as an aid, second, surgeon, umpire, backer or reporter`
    `s 83(1) an act that is none of those in paragraphs (a) to (c)`

@ref Criminal Code s 83(1) (engaging in prize fight) (src:1236-1241)
GIVEN act IS A `s 83(1) act`
      `s 83(2) the encounter is a prize fight: the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83(1) the person takes part in a prize fight` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 83(2) the encounter is a prize fight: the answer` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "prize fight means an encounter or fight with fists, hands or feet" (subsection (2))
        IF act EQUALS `s 83(1) an act that is none of those in paragraphs (a) to (c)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Every one who (a) ... (b) ... or (c) ..."
        IF `s 83(2) the encounter is a prize fight: the answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the answer of subsection (2) is not given

@ref Criminal Code s 83(1) (the offence is punishable on summary conviction) (src:1236-1241)
`s 83(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- The penalty is not stated here: s 787(1) is the seam input.
@ref Criminal Code s 83(1) (punishment) (src:1236-1241)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 83(1) the punishment` MEANS LIST `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`
